@nsobid-41EAE379C103E9A512CFA931BA400E938B3B7C55

# Captain Toad Treasure Tracker 1.4.2 - 2048x2048 shadow resolution

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces the depth shadow map to 2048x2048 (stock DepthShadowParam
// defaults: ShadowMapSize 1024, PrePassShadowMapSize 512; stage archives
// can override them).
//
// al::ShadowDirector::movement is the only caller of
// agl::sdw::ShadowMap::setSize. Every frame it reads PrePassShadowMapSize
// for the light pre-pass shadow types and ShadowMapSize otherwise, and
// the map, its cascade viewports and the shader texel size all follow
// that one value. Both reads become the fixed size.
//
// The map is a Depth_32 texture array of up to three cascades from the
// agl::utl::DynamicTextureAllocator pool, about 50 MB at this size (stock
// about 13 MB). The stock 100 MB pool is sized for native rendering; if
// the game aborts in DynamicTextureAllocator::alloc_, pair this with one
// of the [WxH] resolution mods, which own that pool. Do NOT copy their
// offsets here.

@enabled
003B256C 09008152   // MOVZ W9,#2048 (was LDR W9,[X19,#0x1F0] = PrePassShadowMapSize)
003B2574 09008152   // MOVZ W9,#2048 (was LDR W9,[X19,#0x1D0] = ShadowMapSize)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Captain Toad Treasure Tracker 1.4.2
// (al + agl + sead, NVN). The retail build keeps its symbol table; every
// site was located by symbol and byte-verified against the IDB before
// being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
